.stryker-tmp/
# jscpd HTML report — hundreds of generated files per run, surfaced via
# CI artifact upload instead. The JSON summary is kept regenerable.
reports/jscpd/
# Advisory snapshot regenerated on demand by `pnpm code-health:history`.
reports/code-health-history.md
WORK.md
CLAUDE.md
.playwright-mcp/
# Screenshots from chrome-devtools/playwright MCP dev sessions
/*.png
# Red-team exercise artifacts (findings, threat models, probe scripts,
# evidence logs) stay local. Committing a roadmap of unpatched findings to
# a public repo is its own finding; keep this folder out of git.
.redteam/
# Forensic-report drafts. Reports often name individuals, link wallets to
# real-world identities, and quote on-chain evidence in a form that's
# fine for the team to review in the address book but not a thing to put
# in a public git history. Drafts live here, get reviewed locally, and
# get uploaded to Upstash via the `/forensic-report` skill — not git.
.investigations/

# Review-eval resume caches contain raw model transcripts. Keep them local and
# outside Git and out of any review input. Scored result files live one level
# above.
/docs/evals/review-skill-runs/*/cells/

# clawpatch.ai — review-tool state stays local, not committed.
.clawpatch/

# Arkham marathon — output JSONLs (raw API responses, progress checkpoints).
# Persisted to disk + Vercel Blob; never committed.
.intel-marathon/

# Older checkouts can retain this retired merge-wrapper ledger.
.merge-consents.jsonl

# Backlog ranking receipts and the local exclusion ledger. One run writes one
# dated receipt; committing them would add a file per run and make the ledger
# a merge conflict. See `docs/notes/backlog-ranking.md`.
.rankings/
